// leetcode 2461

interview- In this question, I have to find the maximum sum of a subarray of size K, where all the elements in that subarray must be distinct.

A brute-force approach would be to check every possible subarray of size K and verify whether all its elements are distinct. But that would take more time.

So, I will use the Sliding Window technique along with an unordered map.

First, I will calculate the sum of the first K elements and store their frequencies in the map.

The map will help me check whether all the elements in the current window are distinct. If the size of the map is equal to K, it means all K elements are distinct, because the map stores only the distinct elements.

If the first window contains K distinct elements, I will update my maximum sum.

After that, I will slide the window one position to the right. I will remove the outgoing element from the sum and decrease its frequency in the map. If its frequency becomes zero, I will remove it from the map.

Then, I will add the incoming element to the sum and increase its frequency in the map.

Again, I will check whether the map size is equal to K. If all the elements are distinct, I will update the maximum sum.

I will repeat this process for all the remaining windows and finally return the maximum sum.

class Solution {
public:
    long long maximumSubarraySum(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int n=nums.size();
        long long maxi=0;
        long long sum=0;
        unordered_map<int,int> mp;
        for(int i=0;i<k;i++){
                mp[nums[i]]++;
                sum+=nums[i];
        }
        if(mp.size()==k){
            maxi=sum;
        }
        int i=0;
        int j=k;
        while(j<n){
            sum=sum-nums[i]+nums[j];
            mp[nums[i]]--;
             if (mp[nums[i]] == 0) {
                mp.erase(nums[i]);
            }
            mp[nums[j]]++;
             if (mp.size() == k) {
                maxi = max(maxi, sum);
            }
            i++;
            j++;
        }
            return maxi;
    }
};
